.TH ARO 1 2026-09-26 "aro 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aro \- a minimal tiling Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aro
.RB [ \-s
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-m
.BR logo | alt ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR file | none ]
.br
.B aro \-c
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aro
is a tiling window manager for Wayland, built on wlroots: minimal, flat,
one accent colour, spring-animated.
New windows open beside the focused one, focus moves to the window that is
actually in that direction on screen, and windows can be dragged into place.
Each monitor has its own set of workspaces, created as you use them.
.PP
aro draws its own bar and runs
.BR aropaper (1)
for the wallpaper, so it is usable with no configuration.
The bar steps aside when another bar such as waybar starts.
Its configuration is described in
.BR aro (5);
saving the file applies it at once.
.PP
Run it from a text console, or pick it in a display manager.
Started inside another Wayland session it runs nested, in a window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " command"
Run
.I command
with
.B /bin/sh
once aro has started, after the
.B exec
lines of the config.
.TP
.BR \-m " logo" | alt
The modifier for all bindings, overriding
.B mod
in the config.
Use
.B alt
when running nested, where the outer compositor keeps the Super key.
.TP
.BI \-l " file" \fR|\fPnone
Write the log to
.I file
instead of the default, or not at all.
.TP
.BR \-c " [" \fIfile\fP ]
Check a config file, the default one if none is given, print every problem
with its line number, and exit: 0 if it is valid, 1 if not, 2 if it cannot
be read.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aro/config
The configuration, by default
.IR ~/.config/aro/config .
See
.BR aro (5).
An annotated example is installed as
.IR /usr/share/doc/aro/config.example .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/aro/aro.log
This session's log, by default under
.IR ~/.local/state/aro/ .
The previous session's is kept as
.IR aro.log.old ,
so a crash is still explained after aro starts again.
A nested aro writes
.I aro-nested.log
instead.
.TP
.I /usr/share/backgrounds/aro/
aro's wallpapers, as SVG and PNG.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
aro sets these for the programs it starts:
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The socket clients connect to.
.TP
.B ARO_SOCKET
The socket
.BR aroctl (1)
talks to.
.TP
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
Set to
.B aro
if not already set; it selects aro's portal configuration.
.TP
.BR XCURSOR_THEME ", " XCURSOR_SIZE
The cursor theme and size in use.
.PP
When not nested, aro also hands
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.BR DISPLAY ,
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
and the cursor variables to D-Bus and systemd, so portals started by them
find this session.
On systems without systemd, start aro inside a D-Bus session:
.B dbus-run-session aro
.PP
aro reads
.BR XCURSOR_THEME " and " XCURSOR_SIZE
as defaults when the config does not set a cursor, and the
.B XKB_DEFAULT_*
variables when it does not set a keyboard layout.
.SH DEFAULT BINDINGS
.B mod
is Super, or Alt with
.BR "mod = alt" .
The first
.B bind
line in the config replaces all of these.
.TP
.B mod+Return
Open foot.
.TP
.B mod+d
Open fuzzel.
.TP
.B mod+h/j/k/l
Move focus left, down, up, right.
.TP
.B mod+shift+h/j/k/l
Move the window.
.TP
.B mod+ctrl+h/j/k/l
Resize the window.
.TP
.BR mod+v ", " mod+s
Open the next window to the right of, or below, the focused one.
.TP
.BR mod+tab ", " mod+shift+tab
Walk the window switcher, in recently-used order.
.TP
.B mod+o
Overview: every workspace, zoomed out.
.TP
.B mod+t
Cycle this workspace's layout: manual, dwindle, monocle, scroll.
.TP
.B mod+m
On a scroll workspace, widen the column to the whole screen, or back.
.TP
.B mod+r
On a scroll workspace, step the column through the preset widths.
.TP
.B mod+space
Toggle floating.
.TP
.B mod+f
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B mod+1..4
Go to a workspace.
.TP
.B mod+shift+1..4
Send the window to a workspace.
.TP
.B mod+q
Close the window.
.TP
.B mod+shift+e
Quit, after asking.
.TP
.BR mod+drag ", " mod+right-drag
Move or resize with the mouse; a tiled window tears out of the layout.
.PP
A focused program can ask for these keys itself, as virtual machines and
remote desktops do; aro's bindings then pass to it.
Clicking another window gives them back to aro, and switching to a text
console with
.B Ctrl+Alt+F1
and so on always works.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Attach the output of
.B aroctl log \-\-old
if aro crashed and has been started again, or
.B aroctl log
otherwise, to an issue at
.UR https://github.com/simeulinuxkaliaiwr/aro/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aro (5),
.BR aroctl (1),
.BR aropaper (1)
